# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore -- official-statistics production repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# For: DW sector pipelines (DW-Production and siblings), SDMX /
# data.unicef.org publication pipelines, survey-processing repos.
#
# Template from unicef-drp/cso-toolkit: templates/gitignore/official-stats.gitignore
# Guidance: docs/gitignore_guidelines.md. For papers and analysis projects
# use templates/gitignore/research-project.gitignore instead.
#
# What differs from a research project: there, git is the canonical store
# for results. Here the canonical store is the deposit (Teams / Z:, then
# SDMX / data.unicef.org), and figures are EMBARGOED until their publication
# date: access to this repository is not authorization to release them.
# So output folders are ignored outright (block 1), even a small CSV and
# even its sidecar; after publication, the release PR commits a record of
# what was deposited under releases/<vintage>/ (block 10).
#
# The repo holds code, vendored helpers (00_functions/), the manifests, the
# provenance sidecars of inputs kept out of git, and the release records.
# Check after copying:  git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard  (prints nothing)
# Later rules override earlier ones, so keep the order of the blocks.
#
# Blocks marked [shared] are identical in both templates; the toolkit's
# test suite checks that they stay so. Edit both copies together.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---- 1. Output folders, at any depth: embargoed, never tracked ------------
# Pre-release figures must not reach git, not even as a small CSV, and not
# their .provenance.json sidecars either (hashes and row counts of a small
# table can confirm a guessed figure). Outputs go to the deposit through
# dw_save(). 013_wrkdata is the work-data stage of the deposit layout
# (01_dw_prep/013_wrkdata/<sector>/), where sector scripts write locally.
# `x/**` rather than `x/` so that blocks 2, 3 and 10 can still re-include
# input sidecars, frozen-download sidecars and release records that sit
# under a folder with one of these names.
**/output/**
**/outputs/**
**/results/**
**/wrk/**
**/013_wrkdata/**


# ---- 2. Input folders anywhere (e.g. 02_consultations/023_targets/inputs) --
# Folders are re-included (`!**/inputs/**/`) because git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded; then only these files come back.
# 011_rawdata is the raw-data stage of the deposit layout
# (01_dw_prep/011_rawdata/<sector>/): local copies of raw inputs, same rule.
**/inputs/**
!**/inputs/**/
!**/inputs/**/README.md
!**/inputs/**/.gitkeep
!**/inputs/**/*.provenance.json
!**/inputs/**/input_manifest.*
**/011_rawdata/**
!**/011_rawdata/**/
!**/011_rawdata/**/README.md
!**/011_rawdata/**/.gitkeep
!**/011_rawdata/**/*.provenance.json
!**/011_rawdata/**/input_manifest.*


# ---- 3. API cache and frozen downloads, at any depth -----------------------
# (e.g. 01_dw_prep/011_rawdata/_frozen). A frozen download of another repo's
# output/ folder keeps its sidecars: these lines come after block 1.
**/_apis/**
!**/_apis/**/
!**/_apis/**/README.md
!**/_apis/**/.gitkeep
!**/_apis/**/*.provenance.json
**/_frozen/**
!**/_frozen/**/
!**/_frozen/**/README.md
!**/_frozen/**/.gitkeep
!**/_frozen/**/*.provenance.json


# ---- 4. Data and cache formats, wherever they appear [shared] -------------
*.sav
*.dta
*.rds
*.RData
*.rda
*.parquet
*.feather
*.sas7bdat
*.zip
*.7z
*.gz
*.tar
*.h5
*.duckdb
*.sqlite
*.db
# Check records are always tracked (sh tools/check --record). A ! line
# only overrides the rules above it: keep it after any rule ignoring *.json.
!.checks/*.json


# ---- 5. Secrets and personal configuration [shared] -----------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc
user_config.yml
.Renviron
# A placeholder template may be re-included after this block with an
# explicit `!` line (the official-stats template keeps
# _config_template/user_config.yml that way).
# Do NOT ignore .Rprofile: renv writes its activation line there.


# ---- 6. Tracked configuration -----------------------------------------------
# The placeholder user_config.yml template stays tracked (no real paths or
# credentials in it):
!_config_template/user_config.yml


# ---- 7. Language noise: R, Python, Stata [shared] -------------------------
# R
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/staging/
renv/python/
# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
# Stata
*.log
*.smcl
*.stswp
*.dta~


# ---- 8. OS and editors [shared] -------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.bak
*.swp
*.tmp


# ---- 9. Reviewer-mode artefacts and local copies of the deposit -----------
# A reviewer session writes into its sandbox (sandboxRoot in
# user_config.yml), which holds full copies of canonical and pre-release
# files. Keep sandboxRoot outside the repo; if it sits inside, these names
# keep it out of git (add yours if you chose another).
sandbox/
dw-repro/
# dw_stage() integrity sidecars: local to one reviewer's sandbox, never shared.
**/*.staged.json
# Local copies of the deposit (the Teams 060.DW-MASTER library, a Z: copy):
060.DW-MASTER/
_deposit/


# ---- 10. Release record: tracked, committed AFTER publication -------------
# releases/<vintage>/ holds, per published vintage, output_manifest.csv
# (file, sha256, bytes, deposited_at, deposit_path relative to the deposit
# root) and the .provenance.json sidecars of the deposited files. Commit it
# in the release PR, never before the publication date. Only these files are
# re-included; any data file copied here stays ignored. This block comes
# last so it wins over block 1 for sidecars kept in an output/ sub-folder.
releases/**
!releases/**/
!releases/**/output_manifest.*
!releases/**/*.provenance.json
!releases/**/README.md
!releases/**/.gitkeep
